adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added webhook handler `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the secret check is implemented as a direct inequality comparison:
```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```
This is a plain string comparison (not timing-safe). For shared-secret authentication on a public endpoint, this can leak information via timing differences and is a security defect introduced by the diff.
